{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib proof establishing the sharp additive inequality τ(T) ≤ γ_t(T) + p(T) - 2 for every finite simple tree T on at least two vertices with path cover number p(T) ≥ 2, where τ(T) is the vertex cover number, γ_t(T) is the total domination number, and p(T) is the minimum number of pairwise vertex-disjoint paths covering V(T) (singletons allowed). Because γ_t(T) + p(T) - 2 ≤ γ_t(T) · (p(T) - 1) for all γ_t ≥ 2 and p ≥ 2 (strictly stronger whenever p ≥ 3), this immediately proves all three upstream statements of Written on the Wall II Conjecture 372 in google-deepmind/formal-conjectures (conjecture372, variants.two_paths, and variants.regularized). The formal proof uses an original rooted-tree structural induction certified by a kernel-checked finite-state potential table, bridged directly to Mathlib's SimpleGraph.IsTree and SimpleGraph.vertexCoverNum with only the standard axioms.",
